 and the geometry of inter-\n\nfaces. The present connections between SLE and CFT [2]\n\nfocus on boundary-condition changing operators, which\n\ngenerate the curves. They give d f= 1 + κ/8 for the frac-\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPublications of Pierre Le Doussal (https://www.phys.ens.fr/~ledou/publedou.html)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 11.8 years ago; Critical interfaces in the random-bond Potts model     Jesper L.\nHeight ﬂuctuations of a contact line: a direct measurement of the renormalized disorder correlator     Pierre Le Doussal, Kay Jörg Wiese, Sebastien Moulinet, Etienne Rolley\n    arXiv:0904.4156, LPTENS 09/15 [pdf]\n    EPL 87 (2009) 56001 [pdf]\n\nAvalanche-size distribution at the depinning transition: A numerical test of the theory     Alberto Rosso, Pierre Le Doussal, Kay Jörg Wiese\n    arXiv:0904.1123, LPTENS 09/10 [pdf]\n    Phys. Rev. B 80, 144204 (2009) [pdf]\n\nSize distributions of shocks and static avalanches from the Functional Renormalization Group     Pierre Le Doussal, Kay Jörg Wiese\n    arXiv:0812.1893, LPTENS 08/63 [pdf] [highlight]\n    Phys. Rev. E 79, 051106 (2009) [pdf]\n\nFluctuation force exerted by a planar self-avoiding polymer     Pierre Le Doussal, Kay Jörg Wiese\n    arXiv:0812.1700, LPTENS 08/62 [pdf]\n    EPL 86 (2009) 22001 [pdf]\nChosen for Best of 2009 by the editors of EPL.\n\nCritical interfaces in the random-bond Potts model     Jesper L. Jacobsen, Pierre Le Doussal, Marco Picco, Raoul Santachiara, Kay Jörg Wiese\n    arXiv:0809.3985, LPTENS 08/54 [pdf]\n    Phys. Rev. Lett. 102 (2009) 070601 [pdf]\n\nDriven particle in a random landscape: disorder correlator, avalanche distribution and extreme value statistics of records     Pierre Le Doussal, Kay Jörg Wiese\n    arXiv:0808.3217, LPTENS 08/52 [pdf]\n    Phys. Rev. E 79 (2009) 051105 [pdf]\n\nField theory conjecture for loop-erased random walks     Andrei A. Fedorenko, Pierre Le Doussal, Kay 