601 (2009) - Published 19 February, 2009\n\nShow Abstract\n\nWe study geometrical properties of interfaces in the random-temperature q-states Potts model as an example of a conformal field theory weakly perturbed by quenched disorder. Using conformal perturbation theory in we compute the fractal dimension of Fortuin-Kasteleyn (FK) domain walls. We also compute it numerically both via the Wolff cluster algorithm for and via transfer-matrix evaluations. We also obtain numerical results for the fractal dimension of spin clusters interfaces for . These are found numerically consistent with the duality as expressed in putative SLE parameters.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCritical Interfaces in the Random-Bond Potts Model (https://bibbase.org/network/publication/jacobsen-ledoussal-picco-santachiara-wiese-criticalinterfacesintherandombondpottsmodel-2009)\nciteturn1search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; These are found numerically consistent with the duality kappa(spin) * kappa(FK)= 16 as expressed in putative SLE parameters.\",\"archiveprefix\":\"arXiv\",\"arxivid\":\"0809.3985\",\"author\":[{\"propositions\":[],\"lastnames\":[\"Jacobsen\"],\"firstnames\":[\"Jesper\"],\"suffixes\":[]},{\"propositions\":[],\"lastnames\":[\"Le Doussal\"],\"firstnames\":[\"Pierre\"],\"suffixes\":[]},{\"propositions\":[],\"lastnames\":[\"Picco\"],\"firstnames\":[\"Marco\"],\"suffixes\":[]},{\"propositions\":[],\"lastnames\":[\"Santachiara\"],\"firstnames\":[\"Raoul\"],\"suffixes\":[]},{\"propositions\":[],\"lastnames\":[\"Wiese\"],\"firstnames\":[\"Kay\"],\"suffixes\":[]}],\"doi\":\"10.1103/PhysRevLett.102.070601\",\"eprint\":\"0809.3985\",\"file\":\":Users/marco/Library/Application Support/Mendeley Desktop/Downloaded/Jacobsen et al. - 2009 - Critical Interfaces in the Random-Bond Potts Model(2).pdf:pdf\",\"issn\":\"0031-9007\",\"journal\":\"Physical Review Letters\",\"keywords\":\"Disordered Systems and Neural Networks\",\"mon